Usage: nl [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Number lines of files.

Write each FILE to standard output, with line numbers added.
With no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.

Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.

Supports GNU-compatible numbering formats, logical page delimiters,
renumbering controls, and blank-line grouping.

OPTIONS:
  -b, --body-numbering ARG        use STYLE for numbering body lines
  -d, --section-delimiter ARG     use CC for logical page delimiters
  -f, --footer-numbering ARG      use STYLE for numbering footer lines
  -h, --header-numbering ARG      use STYLE for numbering header lines
  -i, --line-increment ARG        line number increment at each line
  -l, --join-blank-lines ARG      group NUMBER empty lines as one numbered line
  -n, --number-format ARG         use FORMAT for line numbers
  -p, --no-renumber               do not reset line numbers at logical pages
  -s, --number-separator ARG      add STRING after (possible) line number
  -v, --starting-line-number ARG  first line number on each logical page
  -w, --number-width ARG          width of line numbers
      --help                      display this help and exit
  -V, --version                   output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
